From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 16:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: disable HW ATF

firmware stops accepting per-station VOW DRR commands after
band stop/start cycles. every UNI_CMD_VOW STA request on
the affected band is rejected with status 0xC0000001, including a
plain VOW_DRR_CTRL_STA_PAUSE with a zero payload, while band level
VOW configuration is still accepted. Reprogramming the VOW engine on
band start does not recover it.. only a full firmware reload does.

mt7996_mcu_add_sta() treats the mt7996_mcu_sta_init_vow() failure as
fatal, so once the firmware enters this state no station can
associate on the band until the unit reboots.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 mt7996/mcu.c |    9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

--- a/mt7996/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7996/mcu.c
@@ -2931,6 +2931,10 @@ int mt7996_mcu_set_vow_drr_ctrl(struct m
 		.omac_idx = mvif ? mvif->omac_idx : 0,
 	};
 
+	/* HW ATF disabled: fw 20260513 rejects per-station VOW commands
+	 * after band restarts blocking association */
+	return 0;
+
 	switch (id) {
 	case VOW_DRR_CTRL_STA_ALL:
 		val |= FIELD_PREP(VOW_DRR_STA_BSS_GRP_MASK,
@@ -3023,6 +3027,9 @@ int mt7996_mcu_set_vow_feature_ctrl(stru
 		.bwc_enable_per_grp = cpu_to_le16(0xffff),
 	};
 
+	/* HW ATF disabled, see mt7996_mcu_set_vow_drr_ctrl() */
+	return 0;
+
 	/* apply every field this command configures */
 	apply = VOW_FEATURE_APPLY_REFILL_PERIOD | VOW_FEATURE_BAND1_SEARCH_RULE |
 		VOW_FEATURE_BAND0_SEARCH_RULE | VOW_FEATURE_WATF_EN |
